014 can't change melds. So plan must accept that one meld is Bamboo Chow. Then hand will be mixed suits/honors.  \n\nFan calculation possibilities:  \n- Dragon Pung (F3 Pung) = 2 fan.  \n- Seat Wind (North = F4) Pung = 2 fan.  \n- Prevalent Wind (West = F3) Pung = 2 fan (F3 is both West Wind and potential Dragon Pung? Wait, F3 is West Wind tile, J1/J2/J3 are dragons. So F3 Pung gives Prevalent Wind 2 fan, not Dragon Pung.)  \n- All Types (W, T, B, wind, dragon) \u2014 I have W, T, B already, wind (F3/F4), dragon (none yet) \u2014 missing dragon for All Types.  \n- All Simples possible if I avoid terminals/honors in final hand (but my hand already has honor tiles F3/F4). So All Simples not possible.  \n- Outside Hand possible if all melds contain terminals/honors (my exposed Chow B1-B2-B3 contains B1 terminal, so qualifies for Outside Hand in that meld).  \n- Mixed Straight possible if I form 123, 456, 789 in different suits.  \nGiven current hand, the easiest way to get 8 fan is aim for:  \n1. Mixed Straight (8 fan)  \n2. Outside Hand (4 fan) + Prevalent Wind Pung (2 fan) + maybe Edge Wait/Closed Wait/Self-Drawn etc. to reach 8.  \nMixed Straight requires three chows: B1-B2-B3 already one (contains terminal, fine). Need second chow like W3-W4-W5 and third chow like T7-T8-T9 (but T9 exhausted), maybe T2-T3-T4. Need those tiles.  \n\nAlternatively, go for hand with Pung of prevalent wind F3 and Seat wind F4, plus outside hand, plus other small fans.  \n\nLooking at tiles available:  \n- W5: 4 left, good for sequence W3-W4-W5 or W4-W5-W6.  \n- T3: 3 left, T4: 3 left, T6: 1 left, T8: 1 left.  \n- F3: 2 left in wall (I have 2, total 4, so 2 more available).  \n- F4: 3 left (I have 1, total 4, 3 more available).  \n\nDiscard choice now: I need to shape hand towards possible patterns.  \n\nValid discards: W4, T2, W3, F3, F4, T7, W7, T5, W6.  \n\nIf discard a W:  \n- Discard W3: breaks possible W3-W4-W5 sequence, but I have only one W3. W3 might be needed for sequence, but W3 is also terminal (1 is terminal, 9 is terminal \u2014 W3 is not terminal). Keeping W3 helps sequence.  \n- Discard W4: similar, breaks W3-W4-W5 and W4-W5-W6.  \n- Discard W6: breaks W4-W5-W6 and W6-W7-W8.  \n- Discard W7: I have a pair W7, breaking pair reduces chance for Pung.  \n\nIf discard honor:  \n- Discard F3: I have a pair F3, breaking pair reduces chance for Prevalent Wind Pung, which is valuable.  \n- Discard F4: I have single F4, reduces chance for Seat Wind Pung.  \n\nIf discard T:  \n- Discard T2: breaks possible T2-T3-T4.  \n- Discard T5: breaks possible T5-T6-T7.  \n- Discard T7: breaks possible T5-T6-T7 or T7-T8-T9 (T9 gone anyway).  \n\nBest discard: eliminate tile that fits least in possible high-fan plan.  \n\nPlan: aim for Mixed Straight (8 fan) and possibly Outside Hand (4 fan) concurrently? Mixed Straight requires chows in different suits, B1-B2-B3 (B suit) qualifies. Then need W suit chow and T suit chow, numbers must be 123, 456, 789 in any order across suits. My numbers: B1-B2-B3 covers 123 in B suit. Then need 456 in W or T, and 789 in the other. I have W4, W6, W7, T2, T5, T7 \u2014 not matching well. Could aim for W3-W4-W5 (345) and T7-T8-T9 (789) but T9 exhausted. So Mixed Straight may be hard.  \n\nMaybe easier plan: aim for All Types (6 fan) + Prevalent Wind Pung (2 fan) = 8 fan.  \nAll Types requires each of W, T, B, wind, dragon. I have B meld, W and T in hand, wind tile F3 or F4, but need a dragon (J) meld or pair. I have no dragon now. Need to draw J tile and make pair or meld. Possible but uncertain.  \n\nAlternative: aim for Half Flush (6 fan) + Prevalent Wind Pung (2 fan) = 8 fan. But Half Flush requires all tiles be same suit or honors \u2014 I have B Chow exposed, so not possible unless I can change meld (cannot).  \n\nGiven this, safest is to keep options open for high-fan patterns: keep honors for Pung potential (F3 for Prevalent Wind, F4 for Seat Wind), keep W tiles for possible sequences, discard a T tile that is less useful.  \n\nT2 and T5 are central tiles, may help form chows. T7 is less useful because T8/T9 scarce. But T7 can pair with my T7? Wait I have only one T7. T7 can be part of T5-T6-T7 or T7-T8-T9. T6 is very few, T8 few, T9 none. So T7 not great.  \n\nW7 pair is good for potential Pung (W7 Pung gives All Simples? W7 not terminal/honor, yes).  \n\nThus, discard a T that is hard to use: T7 is worst among T\u2019s because T8(1 left), T9(0 left).  \n\n**Reason:**  \nT7 has poor sequence potential due to lack of T8/T9; keeping W7 pair is better for flexibility; keeping F3 pair is crucial for Prevalent Wind Pung (2 fan); keeping W3/W4/W6 for possible W sequences; T2/T5 can form chows if drawn T3/T4 or T6. So T7 is least useful tile now. Discarding it preserves more chances for Mixed Straight, All Types, or Outside Hand combos.  \n\n**Answer:** Play T7"}
